p = "temp/jr/report_text.py"
s = open(p, encoding="utf-8").read()
i = s.index("        \"<div class='note'><b>Where the numbers do not fit the pictures, and why.</b> \"")
new = '''        "<div class='note'><b>Where the numbers do not fit the pictures, and why.</b> "
        "(a) <i>Geometry against identity.</i> The delivered graph of B already draws the lanes through most junctions, so a coverage measure (distance to any GT lane point) shows 0.8 whatever the pair head does; the pair numbers (recall 0.18) count a pair only when BOTH keypoints lie within 4 m and 30 degrees of the two GT ends and the pair is the exact GT pair, so a lane that is drawn in the right place but whose ends are matched to other ends counts as missed. "
        "(b) <i>Topo F1 is flat.</i> It pools everything the graph contains; the connectors are a small part of it. A perfect pair classifier on the same keypoints (oracle, both seeds) lifts topo F1 only by +0.016 / +0.019 over the plain graph (the E308 head at p >= 0.5: +0.006 / +0.005), lanes found +0.056 / +0.066, junction recall +0.18 / +0.23, and it LOWERS topo precision by 0.027 / 0.042: the drawn connectors do not follow the GT lanes closely enough, and only 60 % of the curves are wired to a delivered piece at both ends (3504 of 5798). "
        "(c) <i>The number that matches the pictures</i> is the maneuver coverage: a GT maneuver counts as realised when 90 % of its lane points have a delivered point within 1.5 m in the same direction (within 40 degrees). The plain graph realises 50.4 % (junction precision 0.95), the connectors at p >= 0.5 53.8 %, at 0.2 56.2 %, at 0.1 57.3 %, the oracle pair classifier 59.1 %, the oracle with handle scales fitted to the GT 61.5 %. The pair decision can add about five points at most; the rest is lost elsewhere.</div>"
        "<div class='note'><b>Where the rest is lost (E308 seed 0, 5837 GT pairs whose two ends are matched to keypoints).</b> The connector drawn from the TRUE ends follows the GT connector (within 1.5 m for at least 90 % of its points) for 87 % of the pairs with the chord tangent and for 100 % with fitted handle scales: the curve family is not the problem, the scales are worth 13 points (E303). Drawn from the KEYPOINTS (mean position error 1.44 m, 90 % within 2.5 m) it is 66 % with the chord tangent and 73 % with fitted scales: <b>the localisation of the ends is the biggest single loss</b>, next to the ends that are not found at all (the strict one-to-one match finds both ends of only 52 % of the pairs) and the missing wiring. "
        "Where each maneuver type stands (maneuvers with both ends found, perfect pairs): straight 75 %, left 55 %, right 52 %; chord up to 10 m 81 %, 20 - 35 m 59 %, 35 - 60 m 53 %. Right turns and long connectors are the weak classes.</div>")
'''
s = s[:i] + new
open(p, "w", encoding="utf-8").write(s)
print("ok")
